.TH SHADING 1
.SH NAME
shading \- flat shading from one cross product
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/shading
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Shading
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/Shading.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
A sphere of eight rings by thirty-two faces, the upper half blue and the
lower red, lit by the mouse.  There is no shading model beyond a single
dot product: the face normal is the cross product of two of its edges,
normalised, put through the same matrix as the vertices, and dotted with
the light vector.  A face turned away gets a dither of black against its
colour; one facing the light gets a dither of the colour against its
bright twin, which in this palette is the same hue with the intensity bit
flipped.  Two palette entries and a dither give a whole ramp.
.PP
The original dithers by drawing a random number per pixel; this port uses
an ordered pattern of seventeen levels, which gives the same ramp without
the noise.  The 0.03 of slop on every quad is the original's, and its
comment says why: "Gaps appear without this."
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "mouse move"
Move the light
.TP
.B arrows
Turn the sphere
.TP
.B "any other key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/shading.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
